Z||000000||Eric||02-10-2001||12:10 AM||||Hey everybody  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Just want to know what the latest diet craze/fad is.  I'd like to lose some weight, and I'm pretty freaking serious this time.  I guess...  So give me some advice.  I'm going to run the Columbus Marathon this year.  I'm guessing it doesn't count if you roll through the 26 miles  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||9
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||02-10-2001||12:39 AM||||Eric, a few years ago I decided to lose my spare tire ... lol. So I went on a extremely low fat diet. I also cut out most of the carbohydrates....bread, pastry, etc. The secret to my diet was that I always had something to eat in my hand...always. Things like celery, carots, apples, any kind of fresh fruit or vegatable. I ate a power bar for breakfast...a large salad...no cheese for lunch...and a fairly normal supper. I didn't eat at all after 6:00 P.M. I also did a half hour of exercise each day....usually in the morning before work...walk, rowing machine, weights, jumping jack...you know the drill...1/2 hour, no more, of something. I lost 30 lbs. in a month and a half. That was 10 years ago. When I started my diet I weighed 220...I went down to 190...now I cruise at around 212...Maybe I should do it again.......NAW...lol||||reg||6
Z||000002||Eric||02-10-2001||12:51 AM||||I'm eating chips right now.  That's probably the worst thing I could be doing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Carbs are bad, and I'm going to explode!  I think my fat has taken over my brain, and held it hostage.  It's saying, "Eat more chips.  Have more icecream.  Don't do situps".  I'm going to kill my brain!||||reg||1
