Z||000005||hugh||02-10-2001||07:17 AM||||A lot of people are wary of the Adkins diet,but when I used it I lost 23 lbs. eating chicken wings and drinking a light beer when I got hungry at night.For breakfast I would have fried eggs(or eggs cooked any way you can think of)bacon,sausage,any kind of meat.coffee with no sugar and heavy cream.On this diet if you get hungry it's your own fault.The only thing I didn't like about this diet was it's boring.There are only so many ways you can eat eggs for breakfast.I never had my cholesterol checked,but I've talked to a few people who have and besides losing weight their cholesterol went down.The diet is heavy on fats with very few carbs.(about 40 grams per day).Sorry doc(Frontal Lobe) ||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||02-10-2001||09:45 AM||||Forget the fad diets. Speaking from experience, eat less and healthier, reduce your fat and sugar intake, then exercise, exercise, exercise.<P>A little common sense here, ease into the exercise thing gradually if you're really out of shape. When the weather's nice enough, I go for a mile brisk walk on my work breaks once or twice a day. Walking is better than sitting. Take the stairs instead of the elevator, I do that a lot in the winter.||||reg||1
Z||000007||RNGCRSH||02-10-2001||10:26 AM||||Whatever you do dont starve yourself. It is good to eat more like 5 times a day, small meals. About 3 years ago I reached 235 pounds, I am 5'11". Around this time my father, who is very fat had a heart attack the doctor said it was directly linked to the amount of fat around his heart. He had no blocked arteries. <P><BR>Needless to say this scared the hell out of me. I went on a crash diet and tried to starve my self to loose weight. I ended up gaining 10 more pounds in that month.<P>I went to a nutritionist and they put me on a diet that would help me loose weight. I ate 5 times a day. small breakfast, snack, lite lunch, snack, and finaly a normal supper. The key was not to exceed 1500 calories in a day and to have no more than 200 calories from fat. I after 3 months I weighed in at 165 pounds. I have since fell off the wagon and now am back up to 190 pounds but I know this method works and I was never hungry. My bigest problem is I am alergic to many different foods and it makes dieting very borring and difficult for me because of the amount of time I spend traveling for my job.<P>If you realy want to loose weight and keep it off, then go to a nutritionist and have them structure a diet to help you meet your weight goals.<P><p>[This message has been edited by RNGCRSH (edited 02-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Eric||02-10-2001||10:48 AM||||Those are some good ideas.  I don't believe in those fad diets myself, mostly because they seem boring and don't appeal to me.  I tried the Adkins diet for a few hours last year.  The idea of getting away with eating all those fats, it's criminal.  But I really felt bad after eating a meal without any carbs, kinda like there was a brick doing back flips in my stomach, so I quit.  Now I just need the weather to warm up a little bit so I can start mountain biking and running outside again.  I've got a treadmill, and even though it's really painful, I manage to run two miles on it in just over 16 minutes every day.  I lift weights, light weight with high reps, every other day.  Unfortunatly, I still eat like crap, so I don't lose any fat.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Eric_PA||02-10-2001||12:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR><B>A lot of people are wary of the Adkins diet,but when I used it I lost 23 lbs. eating chicken wings and drinking a light beer when I got hungry at night.For breakfast I would have fried eggs(or eggs cooked any way you can think of)bacon,sausage,any kind of meat.coffee with no sugar and heavy cream.On this diet if you get hungry it's your own fault.The only thing I didn't like about this diet was it's boring.There are only so many ways you can eat eggs for breakfast.I never had my cholesterol checked,but I've talked to a few people who have and besides losing weight their cholesterol went down.The diet is heavy on fats with very few carbs.(about 40 grams per day).Sorry doc(Frontal Lobe) </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have seen this diet work, It's amazing. My cousin at one time weighed in at 320 pounds. A year and 1/2 later..... 165 pounds. I don't think it is very healthy, but he did not suffer with any health issues yet. We went out to the bar recently and he got carded. Well what you know, they thought the picture on his ID card was fake. There was so much of a difference in appearance that it was unbeleivable to see it in real life.<P>I think it's time for me to stop hitting the chips and the pizzas flushed down with beer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I'm lucky so far, but the rate I'm going it won't be long.<P>Eric,<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Eric||02-11-2001||12:37 AM||||Wow, that was fun!  I just love crash diets.  Now that it's all over, I think I'll celebrate with a Sam Adams and a chocolate cake.  No really, I'm back down to my ideal weight, seriously.  Stop sending me Jenny Craig type emails; I'm a freaking rail now!||||reg||1
Z||000011||Standard||02-11-2001||02:25 AM||||man, musta crashed like a lead ballon!<P>I never really understood this "carbs are bad" trend.  Of course, I race mountain bikes and have always been told to stuff myself with carbs... carbo-loading is fun  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Helps that I can burn anything off with no problem, too.  Been eating too much bacon and drinking too much beer every weekend for just about the whole winter and haven't gained any weight  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>------------------<BR>Everybody wants a normal life and a cool car.. <B>Most people settle for the car</B><P>I'm not dumb.  I just have a command of thoroughly useless information<BR>        <BR>AOL: LastMinuteBastrd<BR>AIM: SavedByJebus    -- you'll understand if you watch The Simpsons :D||||reg||1
Z||000012||deceler8||02-12-2001||10:21 AM||||Once you come to the realization that you don't have to eat three times a day just because everyone else does and that's the way you were brought up...once you do that staying slim is easy.<P>And never eat past 5:00pm. ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Tigger||02-12-2001||10:56 AM||||I don't know if it's our winters or Playstation, but most people on the average around here are HUGE.<P>I'm no expert, but I think the reason starving yourself doesn't work is because it triggers a response in your body to slow it's metabolism down.  Thus whatever you eat get's stored.  There are a few exceptions (see <I>Clarista Flockhart</I> sp?).<P>I've heard that the "No, finish your plate, and then you can play" can have some bad side effects on kids.  As they grow older they never really learn to know when they are full.  Basically, they'll feel full only when they are finished eating.  I know it's a useful tactic for parents to get their kids to eat brocoli and asparagus, but it makes you wonder, what is it really doing?||||reg||1
Z||000014||LarryB||02-12-2001||12:34 PM||||Carbs are converted by the body into sugar, which is why they're really good if you're going to be undergoing sustained heavy exertion (running a marathon is a good example) within the next few hours. You've got a greater-than-normal amount of fuel readily available but if you don't use it it'll get converted to fat.<P>It's also the reason why diabetics restrict carbohydrate intake.  We do the starch -&gt; sugar conversion right but can't automagically properly handle a lot of additional sugar. <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Standard:<BR><B>man, musta crashed like a lead ballon!<P>I never really understood this "carbs are bad" trend.  Of course, I race mountain bikes and have always been told to stuff myself with carbs... carbo-loading is fun   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Helps that I can burn anything off with no problem, too.  Been eating too much bacon and drinking too much beer every weekend for just about the whole winter and haven't gained any weight   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||stimpy||02-12-2001||01:13 PM||||SMOKE CRACK. Lots of it. Constantly. You'll loose body fat, bone mass and the useless weight added on by those pesky teeth.||||reg||1
Z||000016||DJRice||02-12-2001||04:34 PM||||Stimpy, this time you beat me to the punch!<P>I used to work in sales and maintained a weight of about 250.  (I am 6'2")  When I graduated college I got a desk job and in August of 1999 I started having a sore knee.  I got on the scale and weighed in at 280lbs.  <P>So I did some research and talked with a colleague who had recently started the Adkins diet.  I read the book and decided to give it a try.  By January of 2000 I had gone from 280lbs to 200lbs and a size 40 waist to a 36.  When I saw my friends at Christmas, they swore I was on the crack rock.  It is now Feb 2001 and I float between 200-205lbs.  <P>The crappy part was that it is very expensive to replace a wardrobe, but I gladly did it.  <P>Heres what you need to get started:<P>Dr. Atkins Book "new diet revolution"<BR>George Foreman Lean mean grilling machine<BR>Chicken Breasts (for grilling - not fried)<BR>Bubba Burgers (again, use the grill)<BR>Any type of lunchmeat<BR>Fish - not breaded<BR>Your choice of cheeses (not lowfat because they add sugar)<BR>Bottled water - I guarantee that if you drink alot of beer or colas and you go cold turkey and drink nothing but water, you will drop 10-15 lbs in 2-3 weeks.  Drink lots of water.  <BR>Lots of Veggies - not fruits or starches<BR>Protien Supplement<P>Other things I ate while on the diet: sugar free coolaid, salads w ranch dressing, BBQ with a hot sauce (no sugar); diet rootbeer or diet coke.<P>I think you will find that most any diet will work if you take the time to research it and find out how/why it works and follow the instructions.  <P>As always, check with your doctor before making drastic dietary changes.<P>Good luck.  It helps to have a friend to encourage you or someone that you can work together on the diet with.  <P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6||||reg||1
Z||000017||Eric||02-12-2001||11:44 PM||||The best thing in the world has got to be the ab slider (or variant).  That thing is nuts.  I got drunk one night, and did twenty reps on a dare.  The next day, I woke up and all I could think about was how much my abs hurt.  I couldn't care less that the room was spinning or how I was about half a breath away from puking; I was doubled over from the ripping pain in my stomach from the ab roller.  Ya gotta try it.  It hurts more, the next day, than your worst hangover  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
